+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Http/Validators/PostValidator.ts
+  - app/Models/Post.ts
+  - app/Providers/AttachmentsProvider.ts
+  - config/attachments.ts
+  - config/storage.ts
+  - tests/PostCover.test.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/claude-fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T16:50:04.098Z }
+---
+
+# Post covers are attachments on a private disk
+
+## Context
+
+Authors can give a post a cover image: a PNG or a JPEG of at most 2 MB,
+uploaded on the new-post and edit-post forms, shown on the post page and in
+the posts list. A cover is a file a stranger chose. `public/` is served as-is
+to anyone, so nothing uploaded may land there.
+
+## Decision
+
+Covers use the framework's attachments layer (`bunx guren add storage` and
+`bunx guren add attachments`) rather than a column on `posts` and hand-written
+file handling.
+
+- **Declaration.** `Post` declares one collection, `cover`, with
+  `hasOneAttached()`. Each stored cover is one row of the `attachments` table
+  and one file on the `local` disk, rooted at `storage/app` (and at
+  `storage/app/testing` under `NODE_ENV=test`).
+- **Serving.** Pages receive `coverUrl`, a signed URL of the delivery route
+  `registerAttachmentRoutes()` mounts at `/attachments/:id/:filename`. It
+  serves the bytes as uploaded, under the content type on the row. The URL
+  answers 404 once its row is gone, so a replaced, removed or deleted cover
+  stops being served at once. URLs are valid for an hour.
+- **What is accepted.** The route contract (`PostPayloadSchema`) checks the
+  size, so an oversized cover is refused the way an empty title is, with the
+  error on `cover`. `PostController` then reads the file's leading bytes and
+  admits the PNG and JPEG signatures only. The type a client declares is not
+  consulted: it is a claim, and the sniffed type is what gets stored.
+- **Image policy is `allow`, not `require`.** The controller has already
+  decided the type. `require` would add a full decode as a second gate and
+  refuse a file with a valid signature that the runtime's decoder rejects.
+- **Nothing is saved on refusal.** On create the cover is checked before the
+  post is written, and the post is deleted again if the attachments layer
+  itself refuses the file. On edit the cover is attached before the post's
+  fields are updated.
+- **Removal.** `removeCover=1` on edit detaches the cover. An upload in the
+  same request wins: the checkbox is about the cover the post already had.
+  Deleting a post purges its attachments.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Every post a page receives goes through `Post.withAttachments(records,
+  ['cover'])` first. `PostResource` requires the `cover` property, so
+  forgetting the call is a type error rather than a post that silently shows
+  no cover.
+- `coverUrl` expires. Render it; do not store it or put it in an email.
+- Attachment rows have no foreign key to `posts`. A crash between deleting a
+  post and purging its cover leaves an orphan, which `bun run console
+  attachments:prune` removes.
+- `storage/app/` holds user data: it is ignored by git and has to be on
+  persistent storage, and backed up, wherever the app is deployed.
+- `APP_KEY` signs the cover URLs. Rotating it without `APP_PREVIOUS_KEYS`
+  breaks the URLs already handed out, for up to an hour.
